  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 removes any numeric sales bar: the 5% figure only triggers reporting and risk-based review, so a model above 5% (such as the Hearth 10) is never automatically barred, and sales are never required to stop. S5 makes recall discretionary with no numeric recall trigger, leaving the 8/100k threshold as a notification and investigation trigger only. S1 is strict (24-hour reporting for all overheating or fire events) and S3 and S4 sit inside the acceptable ranges, with a six-year retrofit and 36-month suppression. The S3 new-unit deadline is tied to a calendar date (1 January 2028) rather than months after adoption, so I recorded it as null."
